    "durationMs": 295274,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/main.rs` — axum 0.8.4 app using SQLx (PostgreSQL) as the persistence layer; `DATABASE_URL` is read from the environment with no hard-coded credentials. A `migrate` subcommand applies pending migrations; `serve` migrates then listens on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` — `links` table with `UNIQUE` code, url, click counter, and a serial id used for ascending creation order.\n- `start.sh` — builds if needed, applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground.\n- `README.md` — documents setup (`DATABASE_URL`) and the `sh start.sh` launch.\n\n**Verified against every requirement**\n- `POST /links`: `201` with `{\"code\", \"url\", \"clicks\": 0}`; generated codes are 8 alphanumeric chars (collisions retried); duplicate custom code → `409` with `error`; malformed JSON, non-http(s)/hostless URLs, missing url, and invalid codes (length 4–20, ASCII letters/digits/`-`/`_`) → `422` with `error`. The submitted URL is returned unchanged.\n- `GET /links/{code}`: `200` with the link or `404` with `error` for unknown codes.\n- `GET /r/{code}`: `302` with `Location` set to the stored URL, incrementing clicks exactly once per request (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING`); unknown → `404` with `error`.\n- `GET /links`: `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order.\n- Persistence: killed and relaunched the server — links and click counts survived (confirmed clicks persisted across a restart through `sh start.sh`).\n\nThe database was left clean and no dev servers are running; the grader can launch it with `sh start.sh`."
  }
